fresh-eyes: independent cold reviewer (subagent, no authorship of this branch), full scope of the three commits closing every reader that hung on a named pipe.

Verdict LAND on this tip, 715ed1d.

Three rounds. Round one returned DO-NOT-LAND: the first fix closed two
doors of six, and status, sync --check, add and update all hung on the
same pipe one command after check named it. Round two returned
DO-NOT-LAND: the branch was six commits behind main so the evidence
did not carry, status called a pipe drift where sync said unreadable,
and the scanner guard at the walk dropped the executable-bit and
convention checks so a pipe named payload.sh scanned clean.

Round three verified on the rebased tree, through the real binary. A
served library with a pipe: list, check, show, index all return. A
vendored library with a pipe: status says unreadable, sync --check
skips, check names it. A dev source with a pipe: add refuses through
the hash. A dev source whose SKILL.md is a pipe: add refuses by type.
MCP almanac_get_skill on the served fixture returns bytes.

Mutations, each killed by a named test: collect_files guard deleted,
red at the timeout after 5.02s; collect_problems guard deleted, same;
the pipe report removed from collect_problems, red at 'check did not
name the pipe'; hash guard deleted, red at the timeout; scanner guard
deleted, red at the timeout; scanner report removed, red at 'the
scanner did not name the pipe'; copy_tree guard deleted, red at the
timeout; status arm reverted to drifted, missouri 8 passed 1 failed on
the named transition. The reviewer also confirmed the transition
catches a real hang: with a walker guard deleted the suite fails in
12 seconds rather than wedging.

The copy_tree assertion had passed with the guard removed in an
earlier round because the destination sat inside the tree being
copied. Found by writing the test to fail first; the destination is
outside now.

77 tests, clippy clean, fmt clean, missouri 9 passed 0 failed, 18
steps, 178 assertions.

Follow-ups, none blocking: skill_md_name's guard has no unit test and
is exercised only through add; the dirent type is a readdir snapshot
so a library mutating under the walk still defeats every guard,
closing which needs open(O_NONBLOCK|O_NOFOLLOW) then fstat at each
site; a silent continue on an unreadable dirent type; a missing
cfg(unix) gate on the walker test; manifest.rs reads almanac.yml
ambiently.
